.TH copy 1 "" "copy 1.2.3"
.SH NAME
copy \- Copy files
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcopy\fR [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-d\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR|\fB\-\-destination\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR \fICOLOR\fR] \fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-size\fR \fISIZE\fR [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIINPUT\fR> [\fIMODE\fR] [\-\- \fIREST\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Copy files.
.sp
Copies the input to the output, keeping the file's permissions.
.sp
\&.Lines starting with a dot are escaped.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
<\fIINPUT\fR>
Input file
.TP
[\fIMODE\fR]
Copy mode
.sp
[\fIpossible values: \fRfast, safe]
.TP
[\fIREST\fR]
Arguments passed through
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR, \fB\-\-destination\fR=\fIFILE\fR
Output file, `\-` for "stdout"
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR=\fICOLOR\fR
When to use [colors]: auto or not.
.sp
The colors are disabled when the output is not a terminal.
.sp
[env: COPY_COLOR=]
.br
[\fIpossible values: \fRauto, always, never]
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-size\fR=\fISIZE\fR
Size in bytes
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-force\fR
Overwrite existing files
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
More output, repeat for more
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with '\-h')
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH VERSION
v1.2.3
